{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20","id":1477936,"title":"How do you think House Balor has changed in C20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-02T19:14:49-07:00","id":1477936,"title":"How do you think House Balor has changed in C20?","content":"House Balor was an over the top house of villains in their section of the Lost Houses book, so how do you think that has changed now, especially since they can even be Seelie? I would suggest that their emissaries to prodigals do not necessarily have to mean Black Spiral Dancers, The Sabbat, or Pentex, and they might not even view them as a first choice for allies. Hell, they may hate the factions who are destroying THEIR world as much as anyone. Maybe Silver Fangs, Shadowlords, Verbena, Hermetics, and Dreamspeakers? They want an edge, allies that can aid them in politics and war, but they probably want a world to rule over, and not just a toxic blight or a world overrun with vampires that are bound to see you as food or rivals.<br /> <br /> I would also like to think that the gorier parts, like where they want to enslave every other Changeling that they don't kill with cold iron is probably gone, replaced by a hunger for respect and success in politics, combined with a desire to find any edge they can get to come out of the shadows of better established Unseelie Houses. That proposed unusual alliance that a handful of Balor and Liam had going on in the C20 PG in Appalachia was one example of reaching out and making atypical alliances. <br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts? What do you want from the modern Balorite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T20:32:40-07:00","id":1477938,"title":"","content":"These are all great ideas, but wouldn\u2019t House Balor\u2019s ultimate goal still be to awaken their Fomorian patron, Balor of the Evil Eye? Or has the house rebelled against its progenitor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T01:27:15-07:00","id":1477944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1477938#post1477938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are all great ideas, but wouldn\u2019t House Balor\u2019s ultimate goal still be to awaken their Fomorian patron, Balor of the Evil Eye? Or has the house rebelled against its progenitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were rewriting their story, I would make it so that was impossible to be the case on account that the other Houses are not idiots and would see that coming a mile away. The new Balor would likely come from a violent rebellion from slaves descended from captured sidhe and Tuathan. Or maybe from test subjects that were captured and twisted. <br /> <br /> Their House being named after Balor could be a bitter joke, something to remind them of what/who they overcame, why they are special, and why they are better than everyone else. Or maybe they turned the tables on him and captured their \u201cfather\u201d and used him as an imprisoned secret and House resource, and using him used to be the focus of their House. Or maybe they have some special House gift/destiny if they claim membership with the Fomorian dream as well as the Tuathan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-03-2022, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T06:27:10-07:00","id":1477947,"title":"","content":"Another take on House Balor might be that they see their actions as a necessary drastic measure. The Leanhaun Sidhe want to destroy or at least crush the Earth to free themselves of a curse. House Gywidon (I'll work on spelling later) wants to rule even if they end up destroying everything, and they never correct their mistakes. The Slavic Sidhe and the Norse Sidhe both have basic issues having any sympathy for non Sidhe, and are pointlessly destructive of society. And most of the other houses are either lost in dreams of the Middle Ages or off on a wild tangent. Both the Kithian and the world are in danger of extinction. <br /> <br /> Balor would bring horror, but he's not willing to let the world be destroyed. If several of the Sidhe Houses must be cut off like gangrenous limbs, that's a small price to pay to save both the Dreaming and Humanity.<br /> <br /> As misguided knights desperately seeking to save the world, Balor would be far more deadly and more humanly understandible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T12:28:28-07:00","id":1477965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1477947#post1477947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another take on House Balor might be that they see their actions as a necessary drastic measure. The Leanhaun Sidhe want to destroy or at least crush the Earth to free themselves of a curse. House Gywidon (I'll work on spelling later) wants to rule even if they end up destroying everything, and they never correct their mistakes. The Slavic Sidhe and the Norse Sidhe both have basic issues having any sympathy for non Sidhe, and are pointlessly destructive of society. And most of the other houses are either lost in dreams of the Middle Ages or off on a wild tangent. Both the Kithian and the world are in danger of extinction.<br /> <br /> Balor would bring horror, but he's not willing to let the world be destroyed. If several of the Sidhe Houses must be cut off like gangrenous limbs, that's a small price to pay to save both the Dreaming and Humanity.<br /> <br /> As misguided knights desperately seeking to save the world, Balor would be far more deadly and more humanly understandible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this a lot, but it seems to me that their goals would still make them even worse than the Baali who were just doing sick and horrible things to keep the (Children?) asleep. I like the idea that they are always testing others with adversity as the C20 book seemed to suggest, but having the a byproduct of the end goal be to blanket the world forever in Darkness seems a bit too much for me. At some point, you have to realize even Oblivion is the better option. Maybe their thinking is along the lines of Hunter the Reckoning, where it is too late to stop the coming Age of the Demon Emperor or whatever, and they are trying instead trying instead to zoom the world through that Age as quickly as possible while preserving everything that can be preserved? That way you can have the DARK Balorians and their Shadow Court, while others are trying to preserve artifacts, knowledge, and even benevolent supernatural races.<br /> <br /> Maybe some of them could be a bit like that Highlander: the Animated Series, where the immortals were trying to find all of humanity's lost knowledge after WWIII. Except the Apocalypse hasn't happened yet, so they are trying to establish hidden time capsules of knowledge, investing in technologies that will be most useful in rebuilding the world after it is done getting wrecked, preserving green areas and species, investing in technology that can possible revive extinct species, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T19:12:15-07:00","id":1478180,"title":"","content":"First I must say that their original write-up has the problem of not mixing well with the actual setting. Why are there even Sidhe descendants of Balor to begin with? It makes no sense, and when things like the Thallain and Dark Kin appeared it made even less sense. Original Balor isn't even that interesting a House as it is just over-the-top, Wyrm-like terrorists. Again.<br /> <br /> That said, I currently (I <b>am</b> using them in my chronicle) just ignore the link. Other houses suspect much, and no one knows the actual origin of House Balor outside it, even in Arcadia, making them highly suspect and untrustworthy on level not even other Unseelie Houses are, yet they're still just another bunch of Sidhe as far as anyone can really tell. Their use of Fomorian imagery furthers suspicion, sure, but for each person that takes it at face value there's another that just think they're being edgy and offensive for laughs with many theories in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T01:29:17-07:00","id":1478192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1478180#post1478180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First I must say that their original write-up has the problem of not mixing well with the actual setting. Why are there even Sidhe descendants of Balor to begin with? It makes no sense, and when things like the Thallain and Dark Kin appeared it made even less sense. Original Balor isn't even that interesting a House as it is just over-the-top, Wyrm-like terrorists. Again.<br /> <br /> That said, I currently (I <b>am</b> using them in my chronicle) just ignore the link. Other houses suspect much, and no one knows the actual origin of House Balor outside it, even in Arcadia, making them highly suspect and untrustworthy on level not even other Unseelie Houses are, yet they're still just another bunch of Sidhe as far as anyone can really tell. Their use of Fomorian imagery furthers suspicion, sure, but for each person that takes it at face value there's another that just think they're being edgy and offensive for laughs with many theories in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason there were Sidhe descendants of Balor is that in the Irish myths Lugh was Balor's grandson. Medieval Irish literature has Sidhe who claimed to be descendants of Lugh. On the other things you've got a point. But Sidhe descendants of Balor was the thing they got right about House Balor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T07:50:19-07:00","id":1478209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1478192#post1478192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason there were Sidhe descendants of Balor is that in the Irish myths Lugh was Balor's grandson. Medieval Irish literature has Sidhe who claimed to be descendants of Lugh. On the other things you've got a point. But Sidhe descendants of Balor was the thing they got right about House Balor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but the point is, it makes sense on Irish mythology, not on CtD.<br /> <br /> On Irish mythology Fomorians and Tuatha are distinct <i>tribes</i>, not so much distinct <i>species</i>. <i>Changeling</i>, on the other side, goes to some lengths to define the distinction between those ancient &quot;wilderness&quot; nightmares and the new &quot;civilization&quot; dreams championed by the Tuatha and represented by the Kithain. There's nothing like Lugh among CtD's Sidhe to point out more complex relationships between the tribes.<br /> <br /> So yes, descendants of Balor among the Sidhe makes sense as a nod to the source material, but not after all the changes they made to create their game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T14:19:38-07:00","id":1478237,"title":"","content":"They probably just wanted to retain something from Irish myth and didn't think it through well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-29T16:47:25-07:00","id":1559107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20#post1477936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Balor was an over the top house of villains in their section of the Lost Houses book, so how do you think that has changed now, especially since they can even be Seelie? I would suggest that their emissaries to prodigals do not necessarily have to mean Black Spiral Dancers, The Sabbat, or Pentex, and they might not even view them as a first choice for allies. Hell, they may hate the factions who are destroying THEIR world as much as anyone. Maybe Silver Fangs, Shadowlords, Verbena, Hermetics, and Dreamspeakers? They want an edge, allies that can aid them in politics and war, but they probably want a world to rule over, and not just a toxic blight or a world overrun with vampires that are bound to see you as food or rivals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree, due to the nature of their origins. House Balor claims to have ties to the Fomorians, who were born of humanity's nightmares. Any faction which intends to reduce the world to a nightmarish hellscape, with mortals huddling in the dark for safety, can only serve to benefit them in the long run.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Changeling Way was created out of desperation to avoid being killed by Banality. It's not something the Fey happily submitted themselves to, and there are other houses who still chafe under having to conform to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Autumn world is not their world. It hasn't been their world since the Sundering , when the Dreaming was physically separated into its own parallel reality. House Balor probably hates the current state of the world just as much as any of the other evil factions. If not more so, due to their alien, fey mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-03T00:05:43-07:00","id":1559192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1478192#post1478192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason there were Sidhe descendants of Balor is that in the Irish myths Lugh was Balor's grandson. Medieval Irish literature has Sidhe who claimed to be descendants of Lugh. On the other things you've got a point. But Sidhe descendants of Balor was the thing they got right about House Balor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason there were Sidhe descendants of Balor is that in the Irish myths Lugh was Balor's grandson. Medieval Irish literature has Sidhe who claimed to be descendants of Lugh. On the other things you've got a point. But Sidhe descendants of Balor was the thing they got right about House Balor.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Most of the Tuatha De Danaan were descended from the Fomorians, according to medieval Irish literature. The Dagda was the son of Elatha, a king of the Fomorians, and so his many children, Brigid, Angus, etc., were all the grandchildren of Fomorians. Ogma was the son of Elatha as well. If the sidhe are the descendants of the Tuatha De Danaan, they ALL have Fomorian blood.<br /> <br /> It never made sense to me that if House Balor were the descendants of Lugh, they would want to emphasize their descent from Balor rather than Lugh.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that House Balor originated as a collection of cast-off sidhe from the other houses who were seen as deformed; perhaps their Fomorian blood ran stronger in those individuals, and the sidhe did not like to be reminded that they all had some Fomorian ancestry. The other sidhe houses began calling them &quot;House Balor&quot; as a derogatory term, but the name stuck, and they began using it themselves as a point of pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-04T17:52:39-07:00","id":1559224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1559192#post1559192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My interpretation is that House Balor originated as a collection of cast-off sidhe from the other houses who were seen as deformed; perhaps their Fomorian blood ran stronger in those individuals, and the sidhe did not like to be reminded that they all had some Fomorian ancestry. The other sidhe houses began calling them &quot;House Balor&quot; as a derogatory term, but the name stuck, and they began using it themselves as a point of pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to C20, House Balor proudly display their deformities. They aren't ashamed of their monstrous heritage, they actually revel in it. Their long term goal is even to restore the world to something resembling the age of the Fomorians, when nightmares roamed the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T01:57:13-07:00","id":1559475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1559224#post1559224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to C20, House Balor proudly display their deformities. They aren't ashamed of their monstrous heritage, they actually revel in it. Their long term goal is even to restore the world to something resembling the age of the Fomorians, when nightmares roamed the land.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes sense, for sidhe who have been ostracized by their fellows because of their deformities. They take pride in what other sidhe find offensive, and are a living reminder to all sidhe that they all share some Fomorian ancestry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T17:18:41-07:00","id":1561327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1559192#post1559192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It never made sense to me that if House Balor were the descendants of Lugh, they would want to emphasize their descent from Balor rather than Lugh.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that House Balor originated as a collection of cast-off sidhe from the other houses who were seen as deformed; perhaps their Fomorian blood ran stronger in those individuals, and the sidhe did not like to be reminded that they all had some Fomorian ancestry. The other sidhe houses began calling them &quot;House Balor&quot; as a derogatory term, but the name stuck, and they began using it themselves as a point of pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Balor is a cooler name than Lugh IMO, but I do like your explanation. That would sort of make them the Clan Nosferatu of the sidhe, wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T13:28:04-07:00","id":1561735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1559107#post1559107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree, due to the nature of their origins. House Balor claims to have ties to the Fomorians, who were born of humanity's nightmares. Any faction which intends to reduce the world to a nightmarish hellscape, with mortals huddling in the dark for safety, can only serve to benefit them in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fomorians were born of the nightmares of whatever came before civilization. We're not sure how long ago it was, if we're talking the transition to written records, the transition to agriculture, or the transition to primates. We only know that at some point abstract dreams became possible and the Tuatha were born.<br /> <br /> Also, just as any Unseelie can point to you that while Ravaging is acceptable, doing it too much is stupid, a world full of nightmares isn't just nightmarISH, it needs people capable of dreaming.<br /> <br /> This is the fundamental need shared by all Fae that isn't compatible with other WoD villains: a world with Glamour, no matter how dark. If the world is too hopeless, if people get apathetic, if waking hours are so horrible that a nightmare is still refreshing, if people simply die and so you have less people to dream, those are all fail states for any Fae, even the Fomorians, much less House Balor.<br /> <br /> For their distaste with the Autumn World, they wish either to make it a more interesting place instead of a cesspool of Banality or be able to live in the Dreaming again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T17:58:14-07:00","id":1561750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561735#post1561735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just as any Unseelie can point to you that while Ravaging is acceptable, doing it too much is stupid, a world full of nightmares isn't just nightmarISH, it needs people capable of dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fomorians were doing just fine before the Tuatha showed humanity a better way to live. Why would they be any worse off returning to those ancient days?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561735#post1561735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the fundamental need shared by all Fae that isn't compatible with other WoD villains: a world with Glamour, no matter how dark. If the world is too hopeless, if people get apathetic, if waking hours are so horrible that a nightmare is still refreshing, if people simply die and so you have less people to dream, those are all fail states for any Fae, even the Fomorians, much less House Balor.<br /> <br /> For their distaste with the Autumn World, they wish either to make it a more interesting place instead of a cesspool of Banality or be able to live in the Dreaming again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Fomorians ruled in a time when humanity was in its infancy, comprised of scattered tribes living in nomadic tents and huts.<br /> <br /> These days, there are over 8 billion of us and climbing. I think the Fey will can engage in a bit of global genocide without suffering a major backlash to their Glamour source.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561735#post1561735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For their distaste with the Autumn World, they wish either to make it a more interesting place instead of a cesspool of Banality or be able to live in the Dreaming again.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> But we know a return to the ancient darkness is what the House Balor wants. They're playing nice with the other houses right now, but that's only until such a time as they've built up their power to seize control of the situation.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha showed humanity good dreams. Taught them to have aspirations beyond mere survival. Taught them honor, taught them fair trade, showed them how to love, and all that good stuff.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians were not born from such things. They ruled in an era where it was Might Makes Right. Where humanity cowered at the thought of what might lay in the dark. Where straying off the beaten path was practically a death sentence.<br /> <br /> Fomorians don't care about uplifting humanity. They viewed them as nothing more than food, slaves, or some other manner of plaything; and that's the kind of legacy that House Balor seeks to emulate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T20:46:36-07:00","id":1561752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561750#post1561750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fomorians were doing just fine before the Tuatha showed humanity a better way to live. Why would they be any worse off returning to those ancient days?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, House Balor isn't the Fomorians themselves. The distinction matters, because their needs are that of a Sidhe, not a Fomorian.<br /> <br /> Second, the Fomorians ruled in a time when the whole of the Dreaming was basically them. If we are to take their legend at face value, as we do if we want to imagine their needs, they'll now share the world with a helluva lot more Fae.<br /> <br /> Third, you're willfully ignoring what the other &quot;villain factions&quot; want:<br /> <br /> Wyrm servants want to corrupt, then poison, then kill everything. Their victims are so utterly destroyed they're beyond the capacity to fear. To fear is to think something worse can befall you. The Wyrm gives you the worse do you don't have to worry anymore.<br /> <br /> Pentex in particular oppress by desensitization, making people so used to horrible situations they just carry on without reaction. Banality is their method of perversion.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Vampires can be something because, despite common themes in crossovers, they're way less horrible than the others. Yet they're not much full of Glamour themselves, they usually kill more than keep in constant terror and they have the Kyasid around.<br /> <br /> Infernalists and Nephandi just want to destroy everything. Including the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> As much as House Balor want to rule a world of terror, this is not what those factions offer. What they offer is horror for the reader, but for the characters is first and foremost the death of Glamour itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561750#post1561750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fomorians ruled in a time when humanity was in its infancy, comprised of scattered tribes living in nomadic tents and huts.<br /> <br /> These days, there are over 8 billion of us and climbing. I think the Fey will can engage in a bit of global genocide without suffering a major backlash to their Glamour source.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was only the Fomorians, sure.<br /> <br /> Also if they think it's worth it, because they did fine without a genocide before, and now more people means more Glamour.<br /> <br /> But again, anyway, this is not the Fomorians.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561750#post1561750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we know a return to the ancient darkness is what the House Balor wants. They're playing nice with the other houses right now, but that's only until such a time as they've built up their power to seize control of the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe.<br /> <br /> This was their old lore, but the thread is specifically about what the new lore may be, how they may have changed from the old, sincerely inane lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561750#post1561750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tuatha showed humanity good dreams. Taught them to have aspirations beyond mere survival. Taught them honor, taught them fair trade, showed them how to love, and all that good stuff.<br /> <br /> The Fomorians were not born from such things. They ruled in an era where it was Might Makes Right. Where humanity cowered at the thought of what might lay in the dark. Where straying off the beaten path was practically a death sentence.<br /> <br /> Fomorians don't care about uplifting humanity. They viewed them as nothing more than food, slaves, or some other manner of plaything; and that's the kind of legacy that House Balor seeks to emulate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, so what?<br /> <br /> Setting aside that &quot;emulating&quot; doesn't imply repetition, a humanity that serves as food for the Fae, as slaves and playthings, is still a humanity that requires basic needs to be fulfilled.<br /> <br /> After all, the Fomorians did not rule a world dominated by the Wyrm. Quite the opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T07:38:42-07:00","id":1561766,"title":"","content":"Monteparnas has the winning argument here. House Balor is facing the same problem as European Fascists and Conservative Monarchists faced in 1941. In all practical terms the Nazis had won, and most of Europe was ready to make deals with them. The problem was that the Nazis weren't just ordinarily evil, they were extraordinarily evil. You couldn't do a business with them. Similarly House Leanhaun, the Wrym, the Oblivion, the Fomori, and Nephandi are all far to evil to work with. The Balor could cut a pragmatic deal with the Sabbat. Both of those groups need humanity able to survive and provide them with entertainment and nourishment. Misery works, total destruction ends the game. <br /> <br /> Balor Shide need to ruin/destroy selected individuals, but they need humanity as a whole to continue to survive and have hope and dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T03:06:37-07:00","id":1561923,"title":"","content":"The main problem with original House Balor is the same problem with original Adhene, Shadow Court and some other groups in the game: authors that don't get it and try to add horror, causing what I call Changeling's 50 Shades of Nightmare<br /> <br /> A lot of people, and that included so many authors, thought Changeling was too much whimsy and lacked teeth, so they added very dark villains.<br /> <br /> Which never changed anything and the game remained looking light and whimsical, and then the next one added another dark villain.<br /> <br /> Most didn't get that the core book alone already have nightmarish lovecraftian gods of a primal world forgotten to Humanity and the character option of starting play as a psychotic killer with unending hunger and bottomless pit for a stomach that literally eat living children as appetizers in parties without any consequence.<br /> <br /> Changeling's horror is precisely being a society of entities to whom the most abject evil is just a valid way of life. It's the only gameline in WoD that has absolutely no mechanically or socially enforced moral standard beyond being bigger than life in anything you do, where the thing the most immoral have to fear is only the reaction of equally uncontrollable 'heroes' with no grasp of consequences for their actions.<br /> <br /> House Balor is cool in many ways. Being dark servants of the Fomorians isn't one of them, it's just generic evil. Allying with all those WoD evil parties is something any Changeling can do. Trying to conquer the world through tyranny is a regular Unseelie activity. Killing other fairies with Cold Iron is the whole plot of the war in the 70s. Adding <b><i>Edgy GrimDark Edginess of Ultimate Evil</i></b> is a fool's errand in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T09:41:23-07:00","id":1561931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561766#post1561766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Balor Shide need to ruin/destroy selected individuals, but they need humanity as a whole to continue to survive and have hope and dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps my use of the word <i>&quot;genocide&quot;</i> gave the wrong impression.<br /> <br /> I meant to say <i>&quot;culling.&quot;</i> House Balor can afford a global culling of humanity, due to the sheer volume in population density. Let's throw a random number out there and say that they managed to exterminate 100 million humans. Well, that's still in the realm of 7 billion, 900 million humans that could sustain them with Glamour. The death toll may as well be considered a drop in the bucket at that point.<br /> <br /> And it's not like this is the first time the Fae have considered such a course of action. Nor are they they only splat to do so.<br /> <br /> Werewolves had their Impergium, and even the Mages considered trying to cut down the Sleeper population in order to shift Consensus back into their favor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Maybe it's because my information came from C20, but aside from working with the Thallain, the Shadow Court didn't really seem all that terrible. One of their stated goals was to restore the old tradition of the Seeliee and Unseelie courts sharing power, instead of allowing the Seelie court to hoard it all year round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T13:30:42-07:00","id":1561932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561931#post1561931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Maybe it's because my information came from C20, but aside from working with the Thallain, the Shadow Court didn't really seem all that terrible. One of their stated goals was to restore the old tradition of the Seeliee and Unseelie courts sharing power, instead of allowing the Seelie court to hoard it all year round.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because C20 took care to explore and reinforce other themes with them, since they would otherwise end up with 4 or 5 identical themes in the book.<br /> <br /> Original Shadow Court is an evil conspiracy to ally with the Wyrm in the name of Nightmare. Original Thallain were the Black Spiral Dancers of the Changelings. Original Adhene were the Nephandi/Baali of the Dreaming. A number of Houses besides Balor were originally evil conspiracies using Wyrm or the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Problem being: core book Unseelie Sidhe do all those things pretty well. An Unseelie member of House Fiona is perfectly fine raiding caerns with the BSDs and partying with them in a Hive. Red Caps see vampires as quaint fellows, but too contained. House Eiluned didn't even need a member to be Unseelie to consort with all of those things and practice infernalism.<br /> <br /> So, House Balor as openly tyrants but smart and politically savvy, trying to gain the upper hand while facing hostility and suspicion, and willing to accept minor victories and be part of a society while keeping their bad reputation as a mark of edgy pride is an interesting concept.<br /> <br /> House Balor as traitorous murderers trying to conquer the world in the name of evil gods is not really doing anything interesting. And being able to kill with Cold Iron is not that impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T13:46:18-07:00","id":1561934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561932#post1561932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because C20 took care to explore and reinforce other themes with them, since they would otherwise end up with 4 or 5 identical themes in the book.<br /> <br /> Original Shadow Court is an evil conspiracy to ally with the Wyrm in the name of Nightmare. Original Thallain were the Black Spiral Dancers of the Changelings. Original Adhene were the Nephandi/Baali of the Dreaming. A number of Houses besides Balor were originally evil conspiracies using Wyrm or the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in C20, the Dauntain's reputation didn't change that much. They were presented as being people who were so antithetical to the Dreaming, that simply existing was enough for them to poison the well.<br /> <br /> It described them as being beyond hope of salvation, as not even reincarnation could undo the damage to their Fae spirits. The only way to deal with a Dauntain was to slay them with cold iron and destroy them utterly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T14:19:07-07:00","id":1561937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561934#post1561934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even in C20, the Dauntain's reputation didn't change that much. They were presented as being people who were so antithetical to the Dreaming, that simply existing was enough for them to poison the well.<br /> <br /> It described them as being beyond hope of salvation, as not even reincarnation could undo the damage to their Fae spirits. The only way to deal with a Dauntain was to slay them with cold iron and destroy them utterly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a reason why I didn't include them in the previous post.<br /> <br /> Dauntain aren't evil. In fact, while some are petty, others are quite well intentioned. They're Banal to a fault, not just without imagination, but seeing imagination as undesirable. They're the actual major antagonists in Changeling.<br /> <br /> This is the thing with the Dreaming: all emotion and storytelling is good for the Fae. Villains are necessary. Conspiracies and blood feuds keep a proper Fae society running. All the bastards above are actually upstanding citizens fulfilling their duty to build a brighter future and avert the coming Winter. They're looking the direst threats to Changelings everywhere and saying &quot;not on my watch&quot;.<br /> <br /> But someone who seeks Childlings to send them back to safety at school or home? The nerve, the audacity! Only the blackest heart in a Fae community would dare say that slaying the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan is too dangerous and you should go home, call the authorities and make better use of your time, like doing your taxes early.<br /> <br /> So the danger of Dauntain is that they're actual heralds of the Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:11:30-07:00","id":1561942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561937#post1561937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there's a reason why I didn't include them in the previous post.<br /> <br /> Dauntain aren't evil. In fact, while some are petty, others are quite well intentioned. They're Banal to a fault, not just without imagination, but seeing imagination as undesirable. They're the actual major antagonists in Changeling.<br /> <br /> This is the thing with the Dreaming: all emotion and storytelling is good for the Fae. Villains are necessary. Conspiracies and blood feuds keep a proper Fae society running. All the bastards above are actually upstanding citizens fulfilling their duty to build a brighter future and avert the coming Winter. They're looking the direst threats to Changelings everywhere and saying &quot;not on my watch&quot;.<br /> <br /> But someone who seeks Childlings to send them back to safety at school or home? The nerve, the audacity! Only the blackest heart in a Fae community would dare say that slaying the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan is too dangerous and you should go home, call the authorities and make better use of your time, like doing your taxes early.<br /> <br /> So the danger of Dauntain is that they're actual heralds of the Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the wisdom in that. Every protagonist needs an antagonist to fight against.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there's really nothing for them to do. The story just becomes a <i>&quot;slice of life&quot;</i> adventure at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T07:52:58-07:00","id":1564081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1561937#post1561937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there's a reason why I didn't include them in the previous post.<br /> <br /> Dauntain aren't evil. In fact, while some are petty, others are quite well intentioned. They're Banal to a fault, not just without imagination, but seeing imagination as undesirable. They're the actual major antagonists in Changeling.<br /> <br /> This is the thing with the Dreaming: all emotion and storytelling is good for the Fae. Villains are necessary. Conspiracies and blood feuds keep a proper Fae society running. All the bastards above are actually upstanding citizens fulfilling their duty to build a brighter future and avert the coming Winter. They're looking the direst threats to Changelings everywhere and saying &quot;not on my watch&quot;.<br /> <br /> But someone who seeks Childlings to send them back to safety at school or home? The nerve, the audacity! Only the blackest heart in a Fae community would dare say that slaying the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan is too dangerous and you should go home, call the authorities and make better use of your time, like doing your taxes early.<br /> <br /> So the danger of Dauntain is that they're actual heralds of the Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how related this it's with the topic, but comparing this description of the Dauntain with the one given in C20 really highlights the difference in tone between that edition and the earlier ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T09:34:30-07:00","id":1564086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jose7057</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1477936-how-do-you-think-house-balor-has-changed-in-c20?p=1564081#post1564081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how related this it's with the topic, but comparing this description of the Dauntain with the one given in C20 really highlights the difference in tone between that edition and the earlier ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get it, so I may not have been clear. Care to share what is your take from my post? That would be much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}